print(
    """
READING LOCK

TEST142 asks a stricter question than TEST141.

TEST141:
    donor geometry itself updated z.

TEST142:
    z perturbs a real Qwen block input,
    the actual transformer response is measured,
    and only that response can drive the next z.

Therefore:

    z_t
      ↓
    Qwen block 10
      ↓
    response_t
      ↓
    endogenous donor-span filter
      ↓
    z_(t+1)

Dibek is not in this loop.

The primary semantic quantity remains:

    Delta_TARGET
        =
        cos(z_T, Dibek)
        -
        cos(z_0, Dibek)

A useful target-selective result requires:

    Delta_TARGET > 0
    Delta_TARGET > Delta_ANTI
    Delta_TARGET > Delta_NULL

But even a clean positive result does NOT mean
a permanent concept has been created.

The stronger defensible interpretation would be:

    a target-blind controller can use the model's
    own local transformer response to recursively
    organize an endogenous latent state toward a
    separately held-out semantic direction.

That is the claim boundary of TEST142.
"""
)


